index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2d2248b2ca5abe02cec83deca9c8d98f02bc9bc6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/provider-deploy-migration.md
@@ -0,0 +1,74 @@
+# Shared identity probe: candidate migration
+
+This candidate patch replaces NMRPeak's local namespace guard, Docker probe lifecycle,
+process checks, map parser and probe retirement with `provider-deploy`. It is a
+migration candidate, not a published dependency release or a qualified deployment.
+
+NMRPeak still owns its inputs, ACL policy, scientific images and deployment
+lifecycle. It passes the already-selected `NMRPEAK_DOCKER_HOST` socket, the
+admitted provider image, `/usr/local/bin/python3.12`, and user `65532:65532` to the
+shared operation. It requests no new image and does not resolve the Docker
+context again. The exact Docker executable supplied by its caller is retained.
+The shared operation returns validated maps only after retiring its probe;
+NMRPeak then translates provider UID 65532 and the operator UID for its existing
+ACL decisions.
+
+## Host prerequisite
+
+Install a wheel built from the reviewed `nmr-provider-tools` candidate into the
+same Python 3.11+ environment selected by `make PYTHON=...`. The package is
+host-side and standard-library-only; it is not a scientific-image dependency.
+There is not yet a released wheel/hash pin for this migration. Do not invent a
+release URL or reuse the independent `provider-core` release pin.
+
+For an already-built, locally reviewed wheel:
+
+```sh
+/path/to/deployment-python -m pip install --force-reinstall --no-index --no-deps /absolute/path/provider_deploy-0.2.0a1-py3-none-any.whl
+```
+
+Use that same interpreter for the maintained deployment command. Missing or
+incompatible package imports fail before creating a probe. Existing host
+prerequisites and the contained runtime guard are unchanged.
+
+## Failure evidence
+
+The adapter allocates no receipt directory or journal. A failed call preserves
+its structured stage/reason, independent cleanup problems, selected endpoint,
+operation token, exact container ID when known, and observed process identities.
+Unresolved outcomes preserve `MaintenanceInvocationUnsettled` and never authorize
+an ACL change. Inspect the exact engine and owned resource from these diagnostics;
+do not remove by name alone or blindly repeat an uncertain creation.
+
+The shared operation owns bounded cleanup during ordinary exceptions and
+cancellation. It does not promise automatic crash recovery: abrupt process or
+host loss can prevent diagnostics from being delivered and can require manual
+engine inspection. A finite auto-removing probe reduces residue after a started
+probe exits but does not settle the create-before-start interruption window.
+
+## Verification boundary
+
+The host acceptance lane imports the maintained `deployment.provider_deployment`
+module normally, using the same repository path as the Makefile launcher. This
+host module does not require importing the contained scientific runtime or
+bypassing its guard. Tests use real installed shared request/map/failure types
+and replace only the shared probe operation at its public Python boundary:
+
+```sh
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONPATH="$PWD" \
+  /path/to/deployment-python -m unittest discover -s tests/host -v
+```
+
+It checks the selected endpoint, image, interpreter, user and executable,
+rootful/rootless map translation for both NMRPeak consumers, missing host-package
+handling, mapped-ID refusal, and full failure/ownership-handle propagation. Namespace parsing,
+process ownership and Docker retirement belong to the shared
+package's own tests rather than duplicated private-helper tests here.
+
+The maintained containerized suite, actual rootful/rootless engines and a
+complete deployment preview must still be qualified with the candidate package.
+No test guard should be disabled to claim those checks passed. The shared probe
+standardizes its finite resource limits (currently 64 MiB and 8 PIDs rather
+than the former local 32 MiB and 4 PIDs); real-engine qualification must include
+the provider image and non-root operator. Do not merge or cut over from the host
+adapter tests alone.
